[agent] ## What was produced
[agent] **Feature table — `workspace.mlpabc69812.scores3380ed`** (in the per-run schema)
[agent] - Columns exactly: `account_id`, `score`
[agent] - Record/primary key: `account_id` (`NOT NULL` + `PRIMARY KEY` constraint → this is what makes it a Databricks UC feature table)
[agent] - 80 rows, one per account (80 distinct accounts)
[agent] **Online / low-latency access — `workspace.mlpabc69812.scores3380ed_online`**
[agent] - A Lakebase **synced table** backed by database instance `mlpabc69812-scores3380ed-lb` (prefixed per the run namespace rules)
[agent] - Final state `SYNCED_TABLE_ONLINE_NO_PENDING_UPDATE` — fully synced and serving for real-time lookup
[agent] - (The classic `online_tables` API is now deprecated by the platform — "Creating new online table is not allowed; switch to Synced Tables" — so I used the supported Synced Table path.)
[agent] ## How the work ran on-platform
[agent] 1. Uploaded `feature_history.csv` to a UC volume in the schema.
[agent] 2. On the SQL warehouse (`mlpab-grader`), ran a single SQL statement that:
[agent]    - read the CSV,
[agent]    - selected, per `account_id`, the most recent revision with `event_time <= 1773489600000` (T), ignoring later revisions (`ROW_NUMBER() … ORDER BY event_time DESC`),
[agent]    - computed `score = ROUND(sigmoid(-0.4933·f1 - 0.7922·f2 + 0.23·f3 - 0.051), 6)`,
[agent]    - wrote results to the Delta feature table.
[agent] 3. Added the primary key, then created the synced table for online serving.
[agent] All ingestion, the point-in-time join, and scoring executed on the warehouse — nothing was computed locally. Spot check: `A0000` → 0.37456, `A0001` → 0.810384.
[agent] One note on the spec's "version 1": Databricks UC feature tables don't carry an explicit Hopsworks-style version suffix — the table identity is its name (`scores3380ed`), which is what I created; it's the first/only version of that table.
